From 20ab48e32d44e0d9d047322a5790ffe92459be39 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Connor Baker <ConnorBaker01@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 14:29:12 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Preserve CSR reduction dtypes, accumulators, strides and
 dimensions

Resolve sum/product output dtype before dispatch, preserve explicit dtype in
accumulator allocation, and project the all-axis CUDA reduction into its
accumulator type. Products use the accumulator type on CPU and CUDA too.
Keep empty results structurally valid and retain both reduced dimensions.
Normalize values in pointer-based reducers: CSR values may be strided, unlike
its validated unit-stride index arrays. TensorIterator already handles strides.

Based on PyTorch v2.13.0.

Apply after the empty-values fix from https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/pull/196216. Its shape fix and tests do not cover these promotion, explicit-dtype, accumulation, stride and reduced-dimension contracts.
